.scanner-output/
.venv-docx
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
packages/*/docs/.vitepress/dist/
packages/*/docs/.vitepress/cache/
# playwright MCP --output-dir (P5.6): screenshots/session snapshots, not covered
# distributed .gitignore-template (harness doesn't give out stuff like that) — project,
# connected preset playwright, I have to ignore it myself.
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/settings.json
# personal/local Claude-project settings (rights, defaultMode — may contain
# bypassPermissions; mechanically-specific, We don’t commit to a public repo). Earlier
# caught only global ~/.config/git/ignore — added explicitly for fresh clones/CI.
.claude/settings.local.json
# personal per-project hook overrides (autonomy/mode — must not be committed)
.claude/auto-approve.env.ini
.claude/auto-approve.config.json
.claude/memory.env.ini
.claude/memory.config.json
.claude/run-report.env.ini
.codex/memory.env.ini
# Ephemeral (temporary) artifacts analyst-lessons — mechanically-specific, we don't commit.
# Important files (events.ndjson, audit.ndjson) remain.
.claude/analyst/lessons/ephemeral/
.claude/analyst/**/*.ndjson
settings.local.json.bak
MERGE-PLAN.snapshots/
# Private legacy node config maind (paths to all projects); sample — packages/maind/configs/registry.example.json
config.json
# review-gate: sample check_command/checks[] — preset repository source of truth
# (mechanically-local instance lives outside the repo, V ~/.claude/hooks/review-gate/), Not
# private config — tracks contrary to the rule above (found P9.1, D135 V plan.md).
!packages/harness/configs/claude-code/hooks/review-gate/config.json
# skiller eval runner — generated benchmark of any skill (run provenance, not a manual artifact).
packages/skiller/skills/**/evals/benchmark.json
# Machine-owned allowlist safe-dirs (car path); sample — safe-dirs.example.json,
# read the hook auto-approve (lib/safedirs.py) And CLI `harness safe-dirs`
safe-dirs.json

# Machine-specific MCP-project config: absolute paths to the launcher maind (leakage
# ways + breaks the clone of others). Sample — .mcp.json.example; generates real file
# `maind` (sync/deploy → mcpconfig.write_mcp). .bak — backup from write_mcp.
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.bak
.cursor/mcp.json
.cursor/mcp.json.bak
# Codex project config: `maind sync` adds MCP launchers with absolute machine paths (perplexity),
# so the real file stays local; the portable sample is .codex/config.toml.example.
.codex/config.toml
# Grok project config: same MCP-launcher paths in `.grok/config.toml`; sample is
# .grok/config.toml.example. `[ui] permission_mode` stays user-level in ~/.grok/config.toml.
.grok/config.toml
# Cursor lifecycle: surface modes (How .claude/*.env.ini) — writes `harness hooks --provider cursor`.
.cursor/*.env.ini
# Cursor/Codex hook runtime: tool-telemetry sidecars (harness.hooks), we don't commit.
.cursor/state/
.cursor/logs/
.codex/state/
# Agent launches from cwd inside the package (same sidecar, different root).
packages/*/.cursor/

# Generated maind hook-project scripts (SessionStart/SessionEnd) + their runtime-state:
# writes `maind sync` from templates/health/*; launcher maind resolves in the scripts themselves
# from env MAIND_BIN → PATH (without machine-specific path). We don't commit — How .mcp.json.
.claude/maind-*.sh
.claude/.maind-feature-log.last
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Assembly copies per-package docks (source — packages/<pkg>/docs; cm. scripts/docs-sync.sh)
docs/skiller/
docs/harness/
docs/maind/
docs/analyst/
docs/brain/
docs/orch/

# Domestic research-docks (audits/trackers) — locally, do not publish
# (anchor to root: DO NOT touch the bucket skills/research registry)
/research/
/RESEARCH/
# Local work traces analyst and draft audits: are not planned
# findings/research and should not be included in the public history of the repository.
/.swissknife/
# Dev-clone marker (PLAN3 D13): created by scripts/dev-clone.sh init, never committed.
/.swissknifeman-dev
/audits/
*.bak
*.last


/.p*

# Historical projections of points materialize only by explicit command of the auditor.
.plan-cache/history/
# Project-local Task terminal-admission runtime state (leases and hash-only events).
.swissknifeman/task-terminal/
.swissknifeman/terminal-admission/
.swissknifeman/state/
# Conductor output (observer reports of every run): generated, never an artifact of a plan item
.swissknifeman/orch/
# Raw role streams (review, executor) are megabytes of token logs: they live in .swissknifeman/state/; a plan
# artifact keeps only the short review-verdict.json (gitignore policy entry plan-role-streams).
plans/*/artifacts/**/*.jsonl

# Local-only working documents (never tracked)
/roadmap/
/tasks/
/.cursor/plans/
/tmp/
# Task plan human views are generated by plan.py render; never tracked.
plans/**/views/
.swissknifeman/backups/

# gui frontend build output (npm --prefix packages/gui/frontend run build)
packages/gui/frontend/dist/
